  "kernel": "40d7fb19a3964c4e54326896c78df174bdd6bcc3",
  "kernel_repo": "Aiden-HQ/AidenHQ",
  "notes": [
    "May add authority (grants, writes, roles or secrets) in: engineering, fleet-steward, monitoring. Auto-updates accept it; turn them off to review first.",
    "Engineers read a failed CI job's log and a PR's changed files",
    "Find loops, repeated failures, unclosed work and stale follow-ups",
    "One Engineer replaces the Software, App and Platform Engineers",
    "The reads the Fleet Steward needs (agent jobs, records and cost since, generations, apps.read)",
    "An agent's reply is its job's final message, relayed to the channel the owner wrote from",
    "A job-log download goes only to GitHub's log hosts, and verify-security knows it",
    "Verify-security derives module networks from compiled config and checks jobs in boxes",
    "Verify-security checks admission keeps a private-reads job off the web",
    "The panel-path registry is eval-gated reviewer code",
    "A failed first install isn't re-applied as its own last known good",
    "One carded conn.tool call files one card",
    "Repo-checkout of a local/ repo gets codehost-local's snapshot",
    "A fleet overseer's comment wakes the assignee on any task",
    "Repo-checkout takes the kernel's code host snapshot, not the runner's cache",
    "A Steward's nudge wakes the assignee; Aiden closes his own task",
    "A concurrent once-only write with the same key waits for the first",
    "Any agent comments on the Fleet issues log, and a cp refusal names its agent",
    "A comment posted for someone else is never the owner's words",
    "Host setup changed (ops/setup.sh or ops/vm): an update runs apply only, so running the installer again may be needed (curl -fsSL https://get.aidenhq.ai | sh)."
  ],
  "release": "2026.11.19"
}
